Rational Owned Choice: Finite Algebras of Multiplayer Games

The paper is main.tex; its technical report is tr.tex. The mathematical audit
entrypoints are root Paper.lean (85 main-paper and cited results) and
Report.lean (105 further report statements and proof ingredients). Every theorem
repeats its complete proposition and has a single named library theorem as its
proof. The scope is the entire main paper and the report material its claims
need, rather than every result in the technical report.

Build and verify

Use Lean through elan; lean-toolchain selects Lean 4.35.0. The dependency
versions are fixed by lakefile.toml and lake-manifest.json. Fetch dependencies
and the mathlib cache, then run the checks:

    lake exe cache get
    make check

make check (also make check-lean) runs lake build Paper Report. Warnings are
errors. Each entrypoint ends with #audit_namespace: every declaration in its
namespace is checked transitively against the standard axioms propext,
Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The theorem statements and their proofs are
versioned in Lean; no JSON inventory is required. The optional whole-source
audit is lake build KFOL.Audit, and the independent algebra import-boundary
audit is lake build KFOL.Audit.Algebra. Lean regressions remain under tests/.

To build the manuscripts with TeX Live and latexmk:

    make paper

The PDFs are build/main.pdf and build/tr.pdf. Each document reads the other's
numbering from committed sections/labels-main.tex and sections/labels-tr.tex,
so either builds alone. make paper refreshes these snapshots; commit them after
changes that renumber results. To prepare a source-only Overleaf upload:

    make overleaf

Upload build/overleaf.zip and select either main.tex or tr.tex with pdfLaTeX.
make clean removes build/; Lake's compiled artifacts are under .lake/.

The full repository can also be synchronized with Overleaf through GitHub.
Only Lean/TeX sources, the bibliography, build tools, dependency pins, license
and repository instructions are tracked. The .gitignore allowlist keeps local
notes, auxiliary checks and verification exports out of synchronization.

Artifact and review entry points

    Paper.lean        85 complete main-paper and cited mathematical statements
    Report.lean       105 further audited report statements and proof ingredients
    KFOL/Definitions/ Mathematical semantics, syntax and word formats
    KFOL/Results/     Library theorem assembly and detailed certificates
    KFOL/Algebra/     Independent mathlib-only algebra
    KFOL/Algorithms/  Word codecs and executable algorithms
    KFOL/Complexity/  Native machine runtime, reductions and class certificates
    KFOL/Strategic/   Full-profile SPE and arbitrary-domain public quantifiers
    KFOL/Rounds/      Sealed-round and sequential-equilibrium semantics
    KFOL/Audit.lean   All-source, transitive axiom audit
    tests/            Lean statement, semantics and machine regressions
    main.tex, tr.tex  Main paper and technical report
    sections/         Manuscript sections and committed label snapshots

Read the mathematical vocabulary first in KFOL/Definitions/PaperAlgebra.lean,
PaperGames.lean and Complexity.lean, then follow their underlying definitions.
They are front doors to the semantics, not the whole definition closure.
The previous 140 full statement contracts remain in
KFOL/Results/Certificates.lean under KFOL.Results. Codec, descriptor and machine contracts
belong there and in their implementation modules, while the root entrypoints
state the mathematical results.

GameTheory supports the strategic and rounds branches. Pure algebra and word
definitions do not import it or the machine-complexity libraries; the import
audit checks that boundary. The machine branch uses ComplexityLib's independent multitape Turing
model, with explicit input/output encodings and charged intermediate storage.
GameTheory is pinned to revision 6f1af625b77215dd9e4454e6120275dbd8b61f51
from port/cslib-complexity, ComplexityLib to
054834a4a4e6ac3ec50ed770bacea7fc42eccc7d, and Cslib to
254e30e6d4299c51323aaeaf5f51a4763b375d4a. Lean and mathlib use 4.35.0.

The earlier Std-only development is retired. Its sources and historical
certificates remain available at commit 7014dbb, for example with
`git show 7014dbb:lean/FullAlgebra.lean`; they are not a second current build or
evidence for unfinished report-only results.

Known source refutation

Ghani--Kupke--Lambert--Nordvall Forsberg's "Compositional Game Theory with
Mixed Strategies" (arXiv:2009.06831v1), Definitions 11--12, has finite
counterexamples to the unit law Id;K = K in Lemma 16 (a right unit in the
source's circle notation) and associativity in Theorem 15. Convex closing does
not repair associativity. Do not use those laws as established mixed-game
composition results.

The self-contained argument is in sections/appendix-open-games.tex,
"Finite obstructions to the proposed mixed open-game category". The external
Lean proofs are pinned to GameTheory v1-final, revision
02898a2d8b918f9b106a683420ca78c99867560e:
https://github.com/elazarg/GameTheory/tree/02898a2d8b918f9b106a683420ca78c99867560e/GameTheory/Languages/OpenGame
The archived scripts/check_external_open_game.py and verification/open-game-v1.json
rebuild and audit an isolated checkout at that pin. Do not modify the sibling
GameTheory checkout. This refutes the
specified composition, not probabilistic open games generally. The paper's
closed-round sequential-equilibrium recursion is proved separately.

Auxiliary evidence archive

The independent Python checks, their data, verification inventories and
definition indexes, and their supporting scripts are archived at commit
2099f2560825ab7e1617ecc6ebb6d65fa0f07ecd. Paths to these files in the technical
report refer to that archive. For example:

    git show 2099f25:checks/README.md
    git show 2099f25:verification/audit-guide.md

Existing local copies are ignored and may still be used. They are not required
to build or audit the Lean entrypoints or compile either manuscript.
